        {
          "id": 3417506632,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "This literally ONLY happens on macOS, where QMacStyle produces a more compact native header height than that generic formula. By overwriting size.height() in AdaptiveViewHeader, the override throws away QMacStyle's compact native value and substitutes the larger generic one. Net effect on macOS: a few pixels taller per header.\n\nFixed in https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/merge_requests/25226",
          "author": {
            "id": 2498449,
            "username": "rknall",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Roland Knall",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9e1d973c5007651b2ca47071f80324c2de5349d873e365cf0761df5542dfe382?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/rknall"
          },
